  "answer": "Malicious File Upload is an attack that falls under the category of injection. It involves an adversary uploading a file that can be executed on the server or client-side, potentially leading to unauthorized access or execution of malicious code. The attack is characterized by the ability to exploit vulnerabilities in applications that allow file uploads without proper validation or restrictions on file types. \n\nKey identifiers for this attack include CAPEC ID: CAPEC-17 and MITRE ATT&CK ID: T1190, which relate to the mechanisms and contexts in which these attacks typically occur. Prevention and mitigation strategies can be found in resources like the OWASP File Upload Cheat Sheet, which emphasizes the importance of validating and sanitizing file uploads to prevent such attacks [Source 1][Source 2].",
